# /sdd-knowledge

Purpose:
  Report on the health and trustworthiness of the .sdd/ knowledge graph.
  Extends /sdd-health with knowledge-specific diagnostics: trust coverage,
  candidate pipeline, conflicts, gaps, unused references, and duplicate
  concepts. Supports diff against a previous snapshot to track knowledge
  evolution over time.

Owns: commands/sdd-knowledge.sdd

Description:
  Scans .sdd/references/, .sdd/knowledge/, .sdd/insights/, and
  .sdd/concepts/ to produce a knowledge health report. Detects stale,
  unused, duplicated, and conflicting knowledge. Read-only — does not
  modify any files unless --fix is supplied.

Usage:
  /sdd-knowledge
  /sdd-knowledge --diff
  /sdd-knowledge --diff <snapshot_file>
  /sdd-knowledge --json
  /sdd-knowledge --verbose

Options:
  --diff          Compare current knowledge against previous snapshot
  --json          Output machine-readable JSON
  --verbose       Show per-reference detail
  --fix           Archive deprecated references (requires human approval)

Output:
  KNOWLEDGE HEALTH

    References:        142
    Established:         87
    Validated:           31
    Candidates:          19
    Deprecated:           5
    Conflicts:            3
    Knowledge gaps:       8
    Unused references:   11
    Duplicate concepts:   6
    Stale knowledge:      2
    Unknown status:       4

  Trust coverage:
    low:     24 (trust.low  references)
    medium:   9 (trust.medium references)
    high:     6 (trust.high   references)

  Candidate pipeline:
    candidate:  13
    validated:  5 (promoted this cycle)
    expired:    1 (candidate expired, no promotion)

Knowledge Diff Format:
  + reference.id      newly added
  ~ reference.id      changed (trust / confidence / evidence updated)
  - reference.id      removed / archived
  ! reference.id      conflict detected
  ? reference.id      status unknown / insufficient evidence

  Example:
    + @skill.retry-with-backoff   (candidate to validated)
    ~ @best-practice.kiss         (trust: medium to high)
    - @pattern.legacy-queue       (deprecated)
    ! @architecture.event-driven  (conflict with @architecture.simple)
    ? @skill.async-handler        (insufficient evidence)

Health Scoring:
  health_score  = (established + validated) / total_references
  trust_average   = mean(trust.level across all references)
  gap_ratio       = knowledge_gaps / total_references
  conflict_ratio  = conflicts / total_references

  Status thresholds:
    HEALTHY   — health_score >= 0.7, conflicts = 0
    WEAK      — 0.4 <= health_score < 0.7, conflicts <= 2
    CRITICAL  — health_score < 0.4, conflicts > 2

  AI behavior by status:
    HEALTHY   — proceed, reuse established references
    WEAK      — propose candidate promotion, flag gaps
    CRITICAL  — pause and escalate to human review

Rules:
  [KD1] The command MUST NOT auto-delete or auto-deprecate any
        reference without explicit human confirmation.
  [KD2] Trust levels MUST be derived from evidence_count, not
        from reference popularity.
  [KD3] Unused references older than 6 months MUST be flagged
        for human review.
  [KD4] Duplicate concepts MUST propose a merge target per
        CANONICALIZATION.sdd merge protocol.
  [KD5] Conflict pairs MUST be linked with a conflicts-with edge
        in the knowledge graph.
  [KD6] Diff snapshots MUST be stored in .sdd/runtime/knowledge-diff/.

